{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DTfakcDNfjawLdnE4ge8QR","type":"tool_result","content":"40:- R6: Tests shall make the races of a continuation deterministic: a take refused after a successful replan, the directory released when the claim is lost, the dispatch returning a recorded continuation of its kind, and a cancelled take; the end-to-end resume of a run with a random recorded name and the handoff plan's pending branches are follow-ups (rounds 1 N3, 2 N8; round 1 and 2 of this spec, N2 and N7).\n74:[Omitted long matching line]\n77:A continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume that meets another resume's recorded continuation returns that record, and a handoff its own agent's; a continuation of another kind or agent is refused (D1).\n125:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused, test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n126:- R2 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1)\n127:- R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n128:- R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n129:- R5 [satisfied] (manual, both locales)\n130:- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityACancelledTakeReturnsItsContext, test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory, test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n132:### Known gaps\n146:### Residual risks\n147:L1 above.\n151:- [open] Resume end to end a run whose recorded runtime name is a random one of an earlier engine, reach the handoff plan's pending branches, and pass the dispatch's context to the plans' waits