{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUTXcGaR5cRMPHf9epCV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WkCoAU1LVPAyW4NAnJ6May","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat <<'EOF' > \"$TMPDIR/probe/draft.md\"\ndecision: approved\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N10\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\",\"line\":74,\"summary\":\"Disputes one clause of L1 only: the winner's record or refused replan after a claim-publication conflict is said to need a race the hooks do not reach, but both are in the dispatch (review_dispatch.go:776-784) and beforeContinuationClaim sits just before the claim. A reviewer probe run through go test -overlay used that hook to remove the taken directory and complete a second resume, and passed: the losing dispatch returned the winner's record with two runs and no ledger losses. Behaviour is correct for the winner's record; the refused replan was checked by reading only. The other clauses of L1 are found acceptable.\",\"action\":\"Add a hook-driven test for the claim-conflict winner record and refused replan, and drop that clause from L1.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N11\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\",\"line\":435,\"limit\":\"L1\",\"summary\":\"Remainder of R2-N8, inside L1's clause on the plans' waits: PlanReviewResume (here) and PlanReviewHandoff (delegation_handoff.go:352) wait with context.Background(), so a cancelled dispatch is not honoured there for up to about two seconds. The wait is bounded and starts nothing; the spec tracks it as a follow-up, although the R1 trace does not cite L1.\",\"action\":\"Pass the dispatch context to the plans' waits.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"}\n],\n\"prior_findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"R6 was rewritten (spec line 40) to the delivered races, with the random-name resume and handoff pending branches moved to a follow-up (line 151). Take after replan and claim-failure removal are covered (review_dispatch.go:762-764 and 771-773 in the coverage profile). The recorded-continuation returns still untested are named in L1 (line 74).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"The take path returns ctx.Err() (review_dispatch.go:2246-2248), covered by TestRunContinuityACancelledTakeReturnsItsContext, which passes; the plans still wait with context.Background() (review_run_continuity.go:435, delegation_handoff.go:352), now in L1. Remainder is N11.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N7\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The R6 text (spec line 40) now matches the tests cited in its trace (line 130), which exist and pass under go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run 'RunContinuity|Handoff'; L1 (line 74) names the claim-conflict and plan-level paths and line 151 tracks the two missing tests. The accuracy of one L1 justification is N10.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N8\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2246-2248 now has a non-zero coverage count; review_run_continuity.go:435 and delegation_handoff.go:352 are unchanged and declared in L1. Remainder is N11.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N9\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Spec line 77 now says a resume returns another resume's record, a handoff its own agent's, and refuses another kind or agent, matching continuationKindMismatch (review_dispatch.go:2256-2268) and D1.\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"The eleven files of the subject, with attention to the diff since round 2 (spec requirement R6, limit L1, contract text, execution log, trace and follow-up; the new cancelled-take test); the dispatch continuation, take, claim, wait and kind check, resume and handoff plans, round thread selection and runtime fallback, the race tests and hooks, and coverage of the guards. Ran the focused tests with coverage, an overlay probe outside the repository, go vet on both packages and the planned pose checks.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Checked each clause of L1 against the code and coverage. Verified: runtime directories are created exclusively, claims are exclusive, a lost claim removes only the directory this continuation took, and the claim-conflict winner return works (reviewer probe). Accepted risks are the permission and ledger faults, the plan-internal races and the bounded plan waits; one justification is inaccurate (N10).\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The lost take, lost claim and cancelled take tests pass here. No path was found that shares a directory or re-runs a recorded continuation; the late fallback creates the round's own directory exclusively and removes nothing of the holder's. The bounded plan wait is N11.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Recorded continuations are answered under the plans' kind rules and the spec's contract text now matches.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Mismatched continuations give refusals naming the other run, a cancelled take returns the context error, and a path that cannot be checked counts as held.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The CLI consumers handle recorded and pending continuations; signatures changed only inside package pose, and no production code changed since round 2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A moved checkout is recorded in safety.limitations with its reason and a held path is named in the thread reason.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined record fields and CLI answers: no schema change, earlier records keep their meaning, and new outcomes are those of the plan refusals stated in D1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Read the continuation paths and ran the focused tests and probe; no functional defect beyond the declared bounded wait was established.\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-3baed7630d422e77\",\"rationale\":\"No structural deltas were observed, so there is nothing to map. Exclusive directory creation as the lock and claim-gated ledger reads address R1, D1 applies the plans' kind rules after a lost race, D2 keeps a reserved attempt usable under R3 and records the move, and a single held-path evaluation addresses R4.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The manual paragraph in both locales and embedded copies, unchanged since round 2, states the held-path condition and the late move as the code behaves. The spec's contract text now matches D1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined refusal and reason texts: they name the continuing run or held path, and a cancelled take no longer advises removing a directory.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1, R3, R4 and R6 as amended have passing tests, R5 is in the manual, and R2 rests on L1. The untested claim-conflict return under R1 was exercised by the probe (N10), and the plan waits under R1 are N11.\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The subject's files are those the spec lists. R6 was narrowed during review to what is delivered, with the remainder tracked as an owned and dated follow-up; no behaviour outside R1 to R6 was found.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined runtime name validation, exclusive creation, removal on a lost claim and the unexported no-op hooks: no new input crosses a trust boundary.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"A small kind helper, two unexported hooks following the package's pattern and a direct fallback are sufficient, with no speculative extension. Resumed sessions that depended on the old absolute path would invalidate the fallback of D2.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-3baed7630d422e77\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, observed, no deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with --no-persist; the gap seen in the output tail concerns an HTTP consumer outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran, exit 1: spec not done, no recorded review, and current semantic inputs reported as not represented by a sealed bundle. It cannot pass before the attestation.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran, exit 1 with 'current semantic inputs are not represented by a sealed bundle'; it cannot pass before the attestation of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it. Eight focused internal/cli tests fail in this sandbox, as in earlier rounds where the messages inspected cited /home ownership; the focused internal/pose tests pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it; the same sandbox limitation applies.\"}\n]}\n```\nEOF\ncat \"$TMPDIR/probe/draft.md\" | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli -run 'TestDelegateHandoffContinuesTheAttemptWithAnotherAgent|TestDelegateHandoffRefusesAndIsBounded|TestReviewRoundsRefuseAnIncompleteAccount|TestReviewRoundsSurviveLossesAndResumes' -count=1 -v 2>&1 | grep -E '^=== RUN|^--- |belongs to another user|_test.go:[0-9]+' | cut -c1-200 | head -n 40; git status --short | head -n 5","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5248,"cache_read_input_tokens":234094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5248},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"20b99d6b-caa8-4d3c-b1b8-b752e2b504ed","timestamp":